# _rl_talente.inc - Talents (Umsetzung 13, Phase 4 section 3). Shared by every madam.
# Told in a narrator's voice, so every madam can use them. Plain ASCII only.
{950}{}{People worth knowing about.}
{951}{}{(There are people in the wasteland who would change a house just by walking into it. Most of them don't want to be found.)}
{952}{}{There's a ghoul in Gecko who sings the Silver Garter's old songs.}
{953}{}{Vesper wants to know what became of her hotel.}
{954}{}{Julian Rook from the Golden Globes wants out of his contract.}
{955}{}{Julian is still on Jet. Let's get him off it.}
{956}{}{The woman next door, Abigail Kessler. She used to be a citizen.}
{957}{}{There's a super mutant in Marcus' jail in Broken Hills.}
{958}{}{[Intelligence] Teach Talus to read.}
{959}{}{Back.}

# Vesper
{960}{}{(Evelyn Marsh, called Vesper, sang at the Silver Garter Hotel before the war. For two hundred years she has lived as a ghoul in Gecko and sung only to herself. She would come back to see the hotel. But the road to New Reno runs past Vault City patrols, and they shoot ghouls on sight.)}
{961}{}{[Combat] I'll escort her myself.}
{962}{}{[Outdoorsman] I know a way around the patrols.}
{963}{}{[Science] I'll forge her a Vault City pass.}
{964}{}{(Go to Gecko. She'll be waiting.)}
{965}{}{(Vesper walks through the rooms slowly, touching the door frames.) This was the Silver Garter. People came here to dance. What is it now?}
{966}{}{[Speech] (Tell her the truth. All of it.)}
{967}{}{(Tell her it's a hotel with music, nothing more.)}
{968}{}{(She listens without interrupting.) Then I'll sing for the people who work here, not for the ones who pay. Somebody should.}
{969}{}{(That night she sees the rooms. She sings anyway, but not for you.)}

# Julian Rook
{970}{}{(Julian Rook was the best-known face of the Golden Globes. He's thirty and looks fifty. The studio holds him with a contract and with Jet. He knows how people want to be looked at, and that's a rare gift in a house.)}
{971}{}{[Barter] Buy out his contract. ($800)}
{972}{}{[Gambling] Win his contract at the studio's poker table.}
{973}{}{[Speech] The studio remembers my work. They'll let him go as a favor.}
{974}{}{Take over his contract, and his supply.}
{975}{}{(The contract burns in an ashtray at the Golden Globes. Julian doesn't thank anyone. He's still shaking. He'll need to come off the Jet.)}
{976}{}{(You sign where the studio signed. Julian works for you now, and he gets his Jet from you now. He'll work as long as you deliver.)}
{977}{}{Julian is sweating through his shirt. Without help he'll be back on Jet within a month.}
{978}{}{[Doctor] Three weeks of withdrawal, under my care.}
{979}{}{Myron's antidote. Give him a dose.}
{980}{}{Send him to the detox room at the Slag in Redding.}
{981}{}{(Weeks later Julian looks almost his age again. He works in every house with private rooms, and the guests who come for him come back.)}
# When a relapse nearly kills him (Phase 4, rule 5: a week to save him)
{996}{}{Julian is dying in the back room.}
{997}{}{(Julian lies on a cot, gray, his breath rattling. The girls have put a wet cloth on his forehead. That is all they know to do.)}
{998}{}{[Doctor] (Work on him through the night.)}
{999}{}{(By morning Julian breathes on his own. He doesn't say thank you. He doesn't have to.)}

# Abigail Kessler
{982}{}{(Abigail Kessler was a medical technician in Vault City. She treated an outsider in the Courtyard with Vault medicine and lost her citizenship for it. She lives next door now. She knows which citizens come down the stairs at night. Some of them voted against her.)}
{983}{}{Vault City owes us. Get her citizenship back.}
{984}{}{[Speech] Councilor McClure owes me. I'll ask him to restore her citizenship.}
{985}{}{[Sneak, Lockpick] Break into the Amenities Office and destroy her file.}
{986}{}{Remind her what she did, and who would like to hear about it.}
{987}{}{(A week later Abigail holds a new citizen's card. She reads it three times.) I'll be your doctor. And I'll stay a citizen. Both.}
{988}{}{(Her file burns in the Amenities Office's own stove. Nobody in Vault City remembers what she did anymore, or that she was ever a citizen.) Then I'm free. Let's see what that's worth.}
{989}{}{(Abigail goes pale.) So that's how it works down here, too. I'll do the job. Don't mistake it for anything else.}

# Talus
{990}{}{(Talus was a soldier of the Master. Now he works the uranium mine in Broken Hills. When people started disappearing, everyone looked at the big, quiet mutant. Marcus locked him up. Marcus doesn't believe it himself.)}
{991}{}{I'll find out what really happened to the missing people.}
{992}{}{I'll break him out.}
{993}{}{(Talus will come to this house when he's free. Marcus wants the truth first. The missing people have to be somewhere.)}
{994}{}{(Talus will come to this house. Go to Broken Hills. Marcus will know who opened the cell.)}
{995}{}{(It takes months. He holds the book as if it could break. The first sentence he reads aloud is on a crate: "Handle with care." He laughs for the first time.)}
